{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus","id":1487590,"title":"Some thoughts on Lazarus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-23T07:56:19-07:00","id":1487590,"title":"Some thoughts on Lazarus","content":"So we had that thread talking about our favorite vampires and I figured I'd type out some thoughts I have on Lazarus. He's always been my favorite vampire in the game. He's had a cool history and done a lot of pretty big things. He's had a fairly outsized impact on the setting compared to many other 4th generation vampires. And, looking at what 5th Edition is doing with him and the Hecata, it feels like they're pushing him to become a pretty central figure in the ongoing metaplot. Note that I'm by no means a big 5E fan but I am very interested in where they're planning to take Lazarus.<br /> <br /> So first off, Lazarus has two stated goals. His first is to become a god. Not God like Cappadocius, he's okay with merely becoming &quot;a&quot; god. Maybe he always had that goal in mind, or maybe he came up with the idea while studying with the Setites. He spent a lot of time with them, he learned Serpentis and their magic. Though note that it doesn't seem that he moved onto any of the Setite paths nor does it appear he worships Set. He's definitely not a Setite, but there probably aren't many non-Setites who are more knowledgeable about them than he is. At least he likely buys into the idea that Set is a divine ascended vampire and he probably wants to do something similar.<br /> <br /> Lazarus' other goal is to recreate the Spell of Life designed by Isis and Osiris in their creation of mummies. He must have learned about that and come up with this goal during his time in Egypt. And he may be much, much closer to this goal than most people would think.<br /> <br /> According to the books, the Capuchin is a persona used by three individuals who work closely together. Lazarus, Mahatma (another one of Cappadocius' childer) and the wraith of Japheth (who was another one of Cappadocius' childer). So basically two 4th generation Cappadocians and the wraith of a third 4th Generation Cappadician.<br /> <br /> The Capuchin &quot;found&quot; the Harbringers in the Underworld. The Harbringers were the Cappadocians that had been trapped in the Underworld during the Feast of Folly. Now importantly in 5E Cults of the Blood Gods it's revealed that the Harbringers <i>aren't actually vampires</i>, or at least they aren't regular vampires. Rather they're wraiths inhabiting vampiric bodies. Seemingly, they're somewhat closer to Risen or even Mummies or Wan Kuei. Note that we don't have any hard rules, so the suggestion is to treat them like vampires, just with higher resistance against Dominate but lower resistance against Oblivion rituals that can command wraiths. What happens when you kill one? Does the wraith die and cease to exist? Or does it simply go back to the Underworld to wait until its body is recreated or it can inhabit a new one? If so, they really would resemble mummies (or even Wan Kuei) quite a bit because that's how those guys work.<br /> <br /> My theory is that, rather than &quot;rescuing&quot; the Harbringers, Lazarus used his own version of the Spell of Life (or more accurately a Spell of Unlife) to return the wraiths trapped in Kaymakli to unlife in the bodies of vampires.<br /> <br /> The other fact revealed in Cults of the Blood Gods is that the Harbringers have their own hidden agenda. They plan to murder all of the other vampires descended from Cappadocius - the surviving Cappadocians, the Giovanni, the Samedi and, oh yeah also probably the Nagaraja (poor bastards picked the wrong clan to join). As Lazarus is directly responsible for the existence of the Harbringers, it's likely that he approves and supports their goal to slaughter their clan mates.<br /> <br /> What's driving the Harbringers? Is simply anger and hatred? Or maybe it's due to Lazarus' Spell of Unlife. My theory is that this Spell can only restore existence to the wraith of a vampire using the remains of a vampire from the same clan and same Generation. They can't kill Brujah or Gangrel and use their bodies to free the trapped Cappadocian wraiths, so the only way for the Harbringers to return the thousands and thousands of trapped vampire-wraiths back into the world is through the killing of thousands and thousands of vampires who are members of the Clan of Death. For the Harbingers and Lazarus, the Family Reunion was simply a way to get all of their victims, which were previously scattered across the world, into one place.<br /> <br /> Another note:<br /> At one point in the past the Capuchin approached Augustus Giovanni with information on the whereabouts of the True Vessel (which held Cappadocius' blood and part of his soul and was necessary for Augustus to fully ascend to the Third Generation). The Capuchin claimed that it was located in the library of Ericiyes, but the library was sadly destroyed by Augustus' son Claudius when the latter burned the temple. Augustus killed his son for that failure and then handed his remains over to the Capuchin. But this seems too easy though, too neat and too tidy. Remember that Lazarus shares the Capuchin's identity with Japheth's wraith, and Japheth is the one who created the True Vessel in the first place. So it's very likely that Lazarus did know where the True Vessel was. But why would Lazarus tell Augustus the location? Why wouldn't he take it for himself? The True Vessel is unique, one-of-a-kind magical artifact of immeasurable power. Surely Lazarus would have laid claim to it.<br /> <br /> And if Lazarus has the True Vessel, and if he's diablarized Augustus, then it's plausible that he's able to perform the ascension to Third Generation that Augustus never was. Maybe Lazarus is already a 3rd Generation in full. Maybe that explains why the Hecata are immune to the Beckoning. Or perhaps Lazarus has other goals, ones that could use the power of the True Vessal and Giovanni's blood to exceed even the power of the Third Generation. He has expressed interest in godhood, so who knows.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe let's look a bit closer at the Beckoning because I think the fact that the Hecata do not suffer from the Beckoning is kind of an important detail. There are many possible reasons for this as the book notes. Maybe Lazarus is already an Antediluvian. Maybe the Beckoning can only be used a clan a single time and then that's it. And since Cappadocius used it for the Feast of Folly it'll never work on his bloodline again. Maybe the ritual the bloodlines used to become made them immune to it.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, let's consider another possibility. And note that I'm going way out into Conspiracy Theory territory on this one, but bare with me. What if the Hecata are immune to the Beckoning because Lazarus is the one who is behind the Beckoning? What if he was able to use the True Vessel to trigger the Beckoning? The Beckoning causes many older vampires to go off and fight and die, so we have a lot of old dead vampires from various clans. And Lazarus' Spell of Unlife can only be used to resurrect a vampire-wraith by using the remains of a vampire from the same clan and Generation. So what's the point? Does Lazarus actually know a bunch of wraiths of ancient vampires from various clans that are trapped in the Underworld and would like to return to Earth?<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, actually he does. He totally does! Lazarus, as the Capuchin, had fairly extensive dealings with the Tal'mahe'Ra. A group of very ancient elder vampires from pretty much every clan of vampires. Their city in the Underworld was destroyed and all of those vampires died in the Underworld. Many of them could have ended up becoming wraiths (the nuclear explosion of the city could have been retconned or exaggerated).<br /> <br /> If Lazarus was attempting to use his Spell of Unlife to restore those guys, then he'd need the bodies of a lot of other very old vampires from various clans. And the Beckoning basically provides that. It would also explain why his own clan isn't affected by it - because Lazarus is behind the Beckoning. That could also explain why vampires who leave and engage in the Gehenna War return different and changed - they're different and changed because now they're being possessed by ancient wraiths from the Tal'mahe'Ra.<br /> <br /> So if Lazarus really does have a Spell of Unlife, and if he is now a Third Generation vampire, and if he is using the Beckoning to create an army of ancient wraith-vampires under his control and maybe he's on his way to becoming a god on top of all of that... well shit, sounds like he might as well just declare victory in the Jyhad because what chance does anyone else have?<br /> <br /> Is this all too gonzo for 5th Edition? Oh hell yes. There's no way that's what's <i>actually</i> going on. But there's a lot of pieces there and regardless, it was fun smooshing them together to turn my favorite vampire into the secret puppetmaster who's on the verge of winning Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case though, it's clear that between the weird Harbringer wraith vampires who are planning to murder the other Hecata, and Lazarus possibly possessing the True Vessel and having plausibly diablarized Uncle Auggie, the authors likely have something pretty big things planned for him. I'm looking forward to seeing what that might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-23-2022, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:24:24-07:00","id":1487604,"title":"","content":"Lazarus is certainly an eigma in The World Of Darkness and what his end goals are. I hope that if they have any clan novels that they do have him in a bigger role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T11:21:13-07:00","id":1487625,"title":"","content":"What about Kheminteri? She's trying to recreate the Spell of Life, too, and I doubt she would let some Johnny come lately steal her prize. Especially since her efforts made her the most wanted of all Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T12:17:09-07:00","id":1487640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487625#post1487625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Kheminteri? She's trying to recreate the Spell of Life, too, and I doubt she would let some Johnny come lately steal her prize. Especially since her efforts made her the most wanted of all Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't she also have a habit of impersonating members of other clans and learning about some dirty secrets that they don't want aired.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T12:57:05-07:00","id":1487643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487625#post1487625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Kheminteri?</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK she isn't trying to recreate the Spell of Life. She actually <b>knows</b> the full Spell, had known it for a very long time. She's just crazy enough that the spell is lost somewhere within her mind. Less that she's trying to relearn it and more that her mind holds the prize a lot of people want.<br /> <br /> But ultimately it seems that Kemintiri is as loyal to the Osirian League as she is capable of being with the current fragmented state of her mind, and otherwise seems actually uninterested in the Spell of Life or its use, although she may be involved in the reconstruction and improvement of it that led to the modern Mummies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487640#post1487640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't she also have a habit of impersonating members of other clans and learning about some dirty secrets that they don't want aired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but she also has a habit of ending up believing her own ruses and not exactly keep an easy track of the things she knows.<br /> <br /> Kemintiri is a really wild card, because it is hard to keep track of where she is, what she believes at any given time, and when she will remember any given information, far before you even start to consider the usual deal of true goals and stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T15:40:20-07:00","id":1487655,"title":"","content":"The bad thing about WoD is their endless retcons. They dont like to deal with the consequences of their own stories. Supposing Lazarus would become a &quot;god&quot;, or 2nd gen or whatever, and declare ultimate victory in the Jihad.<br /> <br /> That would mean the end. No more books. No more money.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a limited pool of old 3rd, 4th and 5th gens out there. Each one that is gone is one less revenue to explore.<br /> <br /> Which is why we end up with a bunch of nonsense to have people brought back to life all the time. And I HATE that.<br /> <br /> It means that none of those stories have any real consequences; everything is reversible, even death.<br /> <br /> It's just like comic books. Heroes die all the time... But that doesnt matter at all, because they are always brought back to life.<br /> <br /> That's why I dont like &quot;open-ended&quot; stories (like comics), because once you end up of ideas, the writters will begin to unleash all kinds of silly times - with the worse of all probably being the invariable &quot;time travel&quot;, the universal &quot;Deus Ex Machinae&quot; to retcon everything.<br /> <br /> Oh, and behold! How convinient to have a clan that has exactly the power to manipulate time! That means that, the moment the meta becomes so convoluted to be unsalvageable, this ace in the hole will come into play, you can bet on it.<br /> <br /> The death of Ravnos is perhaps the worse offender here. Yay, so cool, a god-like monster wreaks cataclismic destruction, and is only destroyed by a combination of SEVERAL massively powerful entities - the most powerful Kuei Jins, and finally the full weight of the Technocracy. Heavy weights only!<br /> <br /> And this sets the tone for such a colossal event.<br /> <br /> Or at least it would, because wait! We just trolled you, he's alive in a Yama kingdom trololololol. So... Nah, consequences free.<br /> <br /> And that pattern repeats itself all over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T17:32:39-07:00","id":1487664,"title":"","content":"Who's fault is it really for the &quot;repeating pattern?&quot;<br /> <br /> White Wold <i>DID</i> have an end for World of Darkness and Vampire the Masquerade. They ENDED it. <i>Then</i>, when they tried to start something else (NWod, Reqiuem, etc) almost everyone threw a tantrum saying &quot;We want more Masquerade!&quot; And before anyone says that didn't happen, I was there. I got Requiem when it came out, and when I tried to recruit people for a chronicle, they looked at me like I was handing out cans of New Coke.<br /> <br /> And the last I heard, Yama Kingdoms were a form of afterlife. They're literally called the <i>1,000 Hells</i>. If you're stuck in Hell, are you really alive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T02:12:56-07:00","id":1487705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487664#post1487664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's fault is it really for the &quot;repeating pattern?&quot;<br /> <br /> White Wold <i>DID</i> have an end for World of Darkness and Vampire the Masquerade. They ENDED it. <i>Then</i>, when they tried to start something else (NWod, Reqiuem, etc) almost everyone threw a tantrum saying &quot;We want more Masquerade!&quot; And before anyone says that didn't happen, I was there. I got Requiem when it came out, and when I tried to recruit people for a chronicle, they looked at me like I was handing out cans of New Coke.<br /> <br /> And the last I heard, Yama Kingdoms were a form of afterlife. They're literally called the <i>1,000 Hells</i>. If you're stuck in Hell, are you really alive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tantrum is a strong word, a lot of people genrally just didn't buy requiem and continued using revised. They're not entitled to our money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-24-2022, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:03:48-07:00","id":1487747,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying anyone was entitled to anything.<br /> <br /> I AM saying it's bloody rich to complain about open ended storytelling when the reason the WoD is open ended is mostly because of an outcry when they actually ended it.<br /> <br /> And I know what I saw. When CoD and Requiem first came out, I saw tantrums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:14:44-07:00","id":1487749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487705#post1487705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tantrum is a strong word, a lot of people genrally just didn't buy requiem and continued using revised. They're not entitled to our money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but I have to side with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3201_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3201\" data-vbnamecard=\"3201\">Father Enoch</a> here. Back then and today.<br /> <br /> I do know people that gave it a try, read the books, and simply didn't got interested in Requiem. I did saw people that simply weren't interested as they already had the books on Masquerade anyway and that's that.<br /> <br /> But I also did saw and still see a lot of people that, sorry, just threw and still throw tantrums over it. Tantrums over the WoD having ended and tantrums over the audacity of Requiem existing. People that refuse to read or consider playing Requiem on principle and sheer prejudice. People that never read the books and yet spun criticism with pure vitriol and hate. Many who aren't just satisfied in not playing or reading it, they actively discourage others and attack those who like Requiem.<br /> <br /> This exists, this happen is this very forum, and while they're not entitled to our money, having a right to such stance doesn't make the stance itself less childish, and sometimes actively harmful to others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:33:41-07:00","id":1487752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487664#post1487664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's fault is it really for the &amp;quot;repeating pattern?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> White Wold <i>DID</i> have an end for World of Darkness and Vampire the Masquerade. They ENDED it. <i>Then</i>, when they tried to start something else (NWod, Reqiuem, etc) almost everyone threw a tantrum saying &amp;quot;We want more Masquerade!&amp;quot; And before anyone says that didn't happen, I was there. I got Requiem when it came out, and when I tried to recruit people for a chronicle, they looked at me like I was handing out cans of New Coke.<br /> <br /> And the last I heard, Yama Kingdoms were a form of afterlife. They're literally called the <i>1,000 Hells</i>. If you're stuck in Hell, are you really alive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont have to buy Requiem if I dont want to, it's a different setting, a different game. People may enjoy or not enjoy CoD as they please. I particularly dont, and I didnt and dont care about it, first because to me it sounded as just another money grab, and secondly because <i>in my opinion</i> CoD lacks the 3 things that I like the most about WoD: Vampire the Masquerade, Mage the Ascension and Wraith the Oblivion. CtD I also like, but I wouldnt mind playing CtL if it were WoD. And WtA I never liked, and the Werewolf game from from CoD seems like an improvement - again, in my opinion - but it's not my kind of supernatural splat to explore regardless. And while there are some other interesting thing at first glance - like Prometeans - it's not enough to pick my interest. And I absolutely HATED the concept of &quot;atlantean mages&quot; from their mage line, and I dont care how well thought the rules are, how better the system is, or how good the stories about it are. Mage the Ascension is my all time favorite RPG game, and the Technocracy my favorite organization of WoD. I utterly love the idea of the Technocracy, and I wouldnt change it for nothing in this world, so thanks but no thanks.<br /> <br /> I have no obligation to learn an entire new game if I dont want to. And the authors certanly arent entitled to my money. And I dont have to give it a try if I dont want to! Why would I <b>have</b> to do it? Now, the company wants to launch a new game, that's fine. People wants to play it, that's fine too. But dont expect to DEMAND us to transition to it just because you want to.<br /> <br /> Im a player of Gurps and Pathfinder. What would you think if I started to DEMAND you to play either one if you HATE those games?<br /> <br /> &quot;Ending the world&quot; was a dumb mistake by White Wolf. That's a problem thou for both WoD and CoD are systems that are also settings; you cant just simply create your whole world using the system, because system and setting are intertwined. There's no Technocracy if we were to play a &quot;Dungeon Fantasy&quot; setting. There's no Masquerade in a &quot;vampire apocalipse&quot; upon which humans live in fortified cities, with some settlements controlled by vampiric overlords. Sabbath vs Camarilla exists only if OUR real world exists on top of a hidden supernatural conspiracy. Everything about the system only works in this &quot;Urban Fantasy of Hidden Conspiracy&quot;. If Newton had invented &quot;Principia of Alchemy&quot; instead of his Principia, there would be no Ascension War.<br /> <br /> And the problem is, ANY changes in the Meta-Plot means changes in the setting, which means changes in the SYSTEM. Remember the &quot;Avatar Storm&quot;? Changes in the meta plot literally created changes in the game rules.<br /> <br /> The only solution would be to introduce a &quot;Static World&quot;. Stop with the meta plot. Let the <u>players and STs</u> create their own stories, instead of forcing those on them. Instead of destroying the world (most stupid thing ever, and everybody was saying this before and after WW came out with this nonsense), they should just say: &quot;look, those are the Ventrue, those are the nosf, those are Tremere etc etc, pick one and go fight the Sabbath and torment yourself for being a monster&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, it's far easier to blame the players than blaming the real culprits. And do you know why WW are the ones to blame? Because they wanted to FORCE people to buy their new games, despite all the veheement protests of the entire player base. Because they wanted to milk our money. That's the only reason why they &quot;ended the world&quot;, in the hopes that everybody would buy an entire new setting of vampire books, an entire new setting of mage books, werewolf books and on and on.<br /> <br /> And the only reason they &quot;un-ended&quot; the WoD is because that obviously failed, many many many people didnt even wanted to hear about the &quot;New WoD&quot;, and just simply sticked with their old books. So they decided to continue the line, to at least be able to milk customers a bit more.<br /> <br /> So, dont blame fans for not sticking up to the &quot;time table&quot; of WW that treated their entire fan base as walking wallets with no regards for what the fans wanted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:46:08-07:00","id":1487754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487749#post1487749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but I have to side with <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> here. Back then and today.<br /> <br /> I do know people that gave it a try, read the books, and simply didn't got interested in Requiem. I did saw people that simply weren't interested as they already had the books on Masquerade anyway and that's that.<br /> <br /> But I also did saw and still see a lot of people that, sorry, just threw and still throw tantrums over it. Tantrums over the WoD having ended and tantrums over the audacity of Requiem existing. People that refuse to read or consider playing Requiem on principle and sheer prejudice. People that never read the books and yet spun criticism with pure vitriol and hate. Many who aren't just satisfied in not playing or reading it, they actively discourage others and attack those who like Requiem.<br /> <br /> This exists, this happen is this very forum, and while they're not entitled to our money, having a right to such stance doesn't make the stance itself less childish, and sometimes actively harmful to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, neither you nor him are right on this one. I followed everything that transpired during the &quot;end of WoD&quot;, and what was done was simply absurd, it was a total disregard to the player base. And it was a pure money grab move.<br /> <br /> I have nothing against who plays Requiem or any other CoD games. I just superficially looked it up in the internet and it didnt pick my interesting, althought there are some titles that seems awesome, particularly CtL and Prometeans, but that's not enough for me, and Mage is my favourite, followed by Wraith, so I really have no reason to try it. <b>And Im entirely within my right to do so.</b><br /> <br /> Is there people who really likes Requiem or other titles from CoD? Maybe even prefer them? Good, more power to them. It's also within their right to do so.<br /> <br /> Nothing wrong about the CoD existing, nor about people enjoying it.<br /> <br /> But I do, however, understand the &quot;vitriolic hate&quot; that WoD old timers feels towards the &quot;New WoD&quot;; it's because WW didnt just simply created a new game and said &quot;look, here's some new stuff for you guys to try!&quot;, instead what they did was trying to &quot;MURDER&quot; WoD in order to FORCE people to make the transition.<br /> <br /> So, obviously people got pissed - and rightfully so I add. Many players felt robbed from their beloved game and forced into something that may not been what they would want to play to begin with.<br /> <br /> So again, it's easier to blame the disgruntled fans that felt betrayed, than to blame the corporation that decided to treat their LOYAL fan base as just simple wallets that shouldnt have a right to have independent thought.<br /> <br /> Now, while I do believe that simply having an emotional reaction towards OTHER PEOPLE that plays CoD is misplaced, I do understand what the source of this frustration is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:55:25-07:00","id":1487757,"title":"","content":"Just a small question for both of you: do you guys play Gurps?<br /> <br /> If not, why dont give it a try? <b>What's up with all that prejudice?</b><br /> <br /> If that example doesnt fit, how about Coda? Pathfinder? Shadowrun?<br /> <br /> Or any other systems that YOU guys particularly never took interest in but other people enjoy?<br /> <br /> So, why do you think that people that enjoys WoD should nevessarily have to &quot;give it a try&quot; to CoD if they have zero interest in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T12:15:20-07:00","id":1487760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487754#post1487754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>And Im entirely within my right to do so.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It is, indeed, entirely within your rights to do so.<br /> <br /> Yet, you just wrote three posts (something you have been specifically told by a moderator to not do) where, just counting the times you accuse people of <i>forcing </i>you or something to that effect, there are 8 whole paragraphs. Others use strong words or right up defend that people are justified in <b>hating a game</b>.<br /> <br /> Overall the whole content of the three paragraphs is a very passionate defense of <b>a game</b> against an attack that <b>didn't happened</b> (we are all discussing in a WoD forum as far as I recall), prompted by someone pointing to the fact that people got pissed at another game. And your third paragraph is outright an attack by means of making a spurious comparison.<br /> <br /> Mind you targeted at people that specifically stated they witnessed all those things. I've been a WoD player long before nWoD was an idea, I am one of those loyal fans and I know a lot others with far distinct reactions on what happened, and there are others in the forums. By the way, I also read and tried every other game you cited but Coda, I'll look that up later.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but your reaction is exactly what I understand as a childish tantrum over what happened regardless of the merits of the company's decision. That, mind you, was also within their rights, because they're not a public service with an obligation to create products they don't want because of whatever the fans think they're entitled to demand from the company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T12:53:50-07:00","id":1487763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487749#post1487749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but I have to side with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3201_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3201\" data-vbnamecard=\"3201\">Father Enoch</a> here. Back then and today.<br /> <br /> I do know people that gave it a try, read the books, and simply didn't got interested in Requiem. I did saw people that simply weren't interested as they already had the books on Masquerade anyway and that's that.<br /> <br /> But I also did saw and still see a lot of people that, sorry, just threw and still throw tantrums over it. Tantrums over the WoD having ended and tantrums over the audacity of Requiem existing. People that refuse to read or consider playing Requiem on principle and sheer prejudice. People that never read the books and yet spun criticism with pure vitriol and hate. Many who aren't just satisfied in not playing or reading it, they actively discourage others and attack those who like Requiem.<br /> <br /> This exists, this happen is this very forum, and while they're not entitled to our money, having a right to such stance doesn't make the stance itself less childish, and sometimes actively harmful to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>True I think on reflection it was almost certainly inevitable for a number of complex reasons, what I found interesting was eventually the discussion died down but its still grinding on in v5. I wonder what the difference is. <br /> <br /> I will however maintain most people simply walked away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T13:03:32-07:00","id":1487768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus#post1487590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another note:<br /> At one point in the past the Capuchin approached Augustus Giovanni with information on the whereabouts of the True Vessel (which held Cappadocius' blood and part of his soul and was necessary for Augustus to fully ascend to the Third Generation). The Capuchin claimed that it was located in the library of Ericiyes, but the library was sadly destroyed by Augustus' son Claudius when the latter burned the temple. Augustus killed his son for that failure and then handed his remains over to the Capuchin. But this seems too easy though, too neat and too tidy. Remember that Lazarus shares the Capuchin's identity with Japheth's wraith, and Japheth is the one who created the True Vessel in the first place. So it's very likely that Lazarus did know where the True Vessel was. But why would Lazarus tell Augustus the location? Why wouldn't he take it for himself? The True Vessel is unique, one-of-a-kind magical artifact of immeasurable power. Surely Lazarus would have laid claim to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The True Vessel is believed in universe to be the last remains of Cappadocious blood and soul. However, we get a detailed account of the embrace of Augustus Gioovanni in WW 2805, pg 21-22. (Clanbook Cappadocian). And it is quite clear that the True Vessel contains the blood they tapped out of Augustus, his mortal blood. It is notable that the people who have been in posession of the True Vessel have seemed to be curiously immune to the hostility of Clan Giovanni (Samedi) or had them embark on projects they would approve of (Setites).<br /> <br /> Japeth did indeed create it though, and also seems to have put the clan curse on the Giovanni. He would have known exactly what it contained, unlike Augustus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T13:04:52-07:00","id":1487769,"title":"","content":"Why all the hate on VTR?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T14:19:02-07:00","id":1487778,"title":"","content":"I stand by my opinion that it was &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Coke\" target=\"_blank\">New Coke</a>&quot; syndrome. <br /> <br /> If there's one thing I could call a silver lining, it's that NWoD came out when it did. The internet had yet to fully embrace the dubious art of stoking outrage in 2003-4. Yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T15:15:13-07:00","id":1487790,"title":"","content":"Excellent post, OP. Lazarus has escaped my attention and interest for years, but your passion and scholarship made him interesting for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:11:53-07:00","id":1487795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus#post1487590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we had that thread talking about our favorite vampires and I figured I'd type out some thoughts I have on Lazarus. He's always been my favorite vampire in the game. He's had a cool history and done a lot of pretty big things. He's had a fairly outsized impact on the setting compared to many other 4th generation vampires. And, looking at what 5th Edition is doing with him and the Hecata, it feels like they're pushing him to become a pretty central figure in the ongoing metaplot. Note that I'm by no means a big 5E fan but I am very interested in where they're planning to take Lazarus.<br /> <br /> So first off, Lazarus has two stated goals. His first is to become a god. Not God like Cappadocius, he's okay with merely becoming &quot;a&quot; god. Maybe he always had that goal in mind, or maybe he came up with the idea while studying with the Setites. He spent a lot of time with them, he learned Serpentis and their magic. Though note that it doesn't seem that he moved onto any of the Setite paths nor does it appear he worships Set. He's definitely not a Setite, but there probably aren't many non-Setites who are more knowledgeable about them than he is. At least he likely buys into the idea that Set is a divine ascended vampire and he probably wants to do something similar.<br /> <br /> Lazarus' other goal is to recreate the Spell of Life designed by Isis and Osiris in their creation of mummies. He must have learned about that and come up with this goal during his time in Egypt. And he may be much, much closer to this goal than most people would think.<br /> <br /> According to the books, the Capuchin is a persona used by three individuals who work closely together. Lazarus, Mahatma (another one of Cappadocius' childer) and the wraith of Japheth (who was another one of Cappadocius' childer). So basically two 4th generation Cappadocians and the wraith of a third 4th Generation Cappadician.<br /> <br /> The Capuchin &quot;found&quot; the Harbringers in the Underworld. The Harbringers were the Cappadocians that had been trapped in the Underworld during the Feast of Folly. Now importantly in 5E Cults of the Blood Gods it's revealed that the Harbringers <i>aren't actually vampires</i>, or at least they aren't regular vampires. Rather they're wraiths inhabiting vampiric bodies. Seemingly, they're somewhat closer to Risen or even Mummies or Wan Kuei. Note that we don't have any hard rules, so the suggestion is to treat them like vampires, just with higher resistance against Dominate but lower resistance against Oblivion rituals that can command wraiths. What happens when you kill one? Does the wraith die and cease to exist? Or does it simply go back to the Underworld to wait until its body is recreated or it can inhabit a new one? If so, they really would resemble mummies (or even Wan Kuei) quite a bit because that's how those guys work.<br /> <br /> My theory is that, rather than &quot;rescuing&quot; the Harbringers, Lazarus used his own version of the Spell of Life (or more accurately a Spell of Unlife) to return the wraiths trapped in Kaymakli to unlife in the bodies of vampires.<br /> <br /> The other fact revealed in Cults of the Blood Gods is that the Harbringers have their own hidden agenda. They plan to murder all of the other vampires descended from Cappadocius - the surviving Cappadocians, the Giovanni, the Samedi and, oh yeah also probably the Nagaraja (poor bastards picked the wrong clan to join). As Lazarus is directly responsible for the existence of the Harbringers, it's likely that he approves and supports their goal to slaughter their clan mates.<br /> <br /> What's driving the Harbringers? Is simply anger and hatred? Or maybe it's due to Lazarus' Spell of Unlife. My theory is that this Spell can only restore existence to the wraith of a vampire using the remains of a vampire from the same clan and same Generation. They can't kill Brujah or Gangrel and use their bodies to free the trapped Cappadocian wraiths, so the only way for the Harbringers to return the thousands and thousands of trapped vampire-wraiths back into the world is through the killing of thousands and thousands of vampires who are members of the Clan of Death. For the Harbingers and Lazarus, the Family Reunion was simply a way to get all of their victims, which were previously scattered across the world, into one place.<br /> <br /> Another note:<br /> At one point in the past the Capuchin approached Augustus Giovanni with information on the whereabouts of the True Vessel (which held Cappadocius' blood and part of his soul and was necessary for Augustus to fully ascend to the Third Generation). The Capuchin claimed that it was located in the library of Ericiyes, but the library was sadly destroyed by Augustus' son Claudius when the latter burned the temple. Augustus killed his son for that failure and then handed his remains over to the Capuchin. But this seems too easy though, too neat and too tidy. Remember that Lazarus shares the Capuchin's identity with Japheth's wraith, and Japheth is the one who created the True Vessel in the first place. So it's very likely that Lazarus did know where the True Vessel was. But why would Lazarus tell Augustus the location? Why wouldn't he take it for himself? The True Vessel is unique, one-of-a-kind magical artifact of immeasurable power. Surely Lazarus would have laid claim to it.<br /> <br /> And if Lazarus has the True Vessel, and if he's diablarized Augustus, then it's plausible that he's able to perform the ascension to Third Generation that Augustus never was. Maybe Lazarus is already a 3rd Generation in full. Maybe that explains why the Hecata are immune to the Beckoning. Or perhaps Lazarus has other goals, ones that could use the power of the True Vessal and Giovanni's blood to exceed even the power of the Third Generation. He has expressed interest in godhood, so who knows.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe let's look a bit closer at the Beckoning because I think the fact that the Hecata do not suffer from the Beckoning is kind of an important detail. There are many possible reasons for this as the book notes. Maybe Lazarus is already an Antediluvian. Maybe the Beckoning can only be used a clan a single time and then that's it. And since Cappadocius used it for the Feast of Folly it'll never work on his bloodline again. Maybe the ritual the bloodlines used to become made them immune to it.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, let's consider another possibility. And note that I'm going way out into Conspiracy Theory territory on this one, but bare with me. What if the Hecata are immune to the Beckoning because Lazarus is the one who is behind the Beckoning? What if he was able to use the True Vessel to trigger the Beckoning? The Beckoning causes many older vampires to go off and fight and die, so we have a lot of old dead vampires from various clans. And Lazarus' Spell of Unlife can only be used to resurrect a vampire-wraith by using the remains of a vampire from the same clan and Generation. So what's the point? Does Lazarus actually know a bunch of wraiths of ancient vampires from various clans that are trapped in the Underworld and would like to return to Earth?<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, actually he does. He totally does! Lazarus, as the Capuchin, had fairly extensive dealings with the Tal'mahe'Ra. A group of very ancient elder vampires from pretty much every clan of vampires. Their city in the Underworld was destroyed and all of those vampires died in the Underworld. Many of them could have ended up becoming wraiths (the nuclear explosion of the city could have been retconned or exaggerated).<br /> <br /> If Lazarus was attempting to use his Spell of Unlife to restore those guys, then he'd need the bodies of a lot of other very old vampires from various clans. And the Beckoning basically provides that. It would also explain why his own clan isn't affected by it - because Lazarus is behind the Beckoning. That could also explain why vampires who leave and engage in the Gehenna War return different and changed - they're different and changed because now they're being possessed by ancient wraiths from the Tal'mahe'Ra.<br /> <br /> So if Lazarus really does have a Spell of Unlife, and if he is now a Third Generation vampire, and if he is using the Beckoning to create an army of ancient wraith-vampires under his control and maybe he's on his way to becoming a god on top of all of that... well shit, sounds like he might as well just declare victory in the Jyhad because what chance does anyone else have?<br /> <br /> Is this all too gonzo for 5th Edition? Oh hell yes. There's no way that's what's <i>actually</i> going on. But there's a lot of pieces there and regardless, it was fun smooshing them together to turn my favorite vampire into the secret puppetmaster who's on the verge of winning Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case though, it's clear that between the weird Harbringer wraith vampires who are planning to murder the other Hecata, and Lazarus possibly possessing the True Vessel and having plausibly diablarized Uncle Auggie, the authors likely have something pretty big things planned for him. I'm looking forward to seeing what that might be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really liked your take on Lazarus, there are many interesting ideas in your post. He's also one of my favorite characters in the WoD and, even though I hated 90% of what they did in V5, if they do something interesting with him, I'll certainly enjoy reading. I'm just hoping V5 won't ruin him as they did with more than half the setting. Also, the new bloodline seems much more interesting than &quot;Italian mafia&quot; to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T04:46:01-07:00","id":1487862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487778#post1487778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand by my opinion that it was &amp;quot;<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Coke&amp;quot;]New</a> Coke[/URL]&amp;quot; syndrome. <br /> <br /> If there's one thing I could call a silver lining, it's that NWoD came out when it did. The internet had yet to fully embrace the dubious art of stoking outrage in 2003-4. Yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people are just uninterested. Or it's just a matter of habit too. If you're used to the same old same old, most of the time you dont wanna try the new. No biggie.<br /> <br /> But like I said, the hate in my opinion is because many people felt scammed. It seemed like WW wanted to destroy WoD to shove the NWoD down on everybody's throats. And people get, lets say, &quot;sensitive&quot; when they feel they are being pushed around.<br /> <br /> It was a bad move from the part of the company. Had they just introduced CoD as a different line Im sure this wouldnt happen, and the worse reaction would just simply be a &quot;not my thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, they did what they did, it is what is and now there is this stigma to it and that dumb rivalry between A FEW people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T04:49:55-07:00","id":1487863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487768#post1487768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The True Vessel is believed in universe to be the last remains of Cappadocious blood and soul. However, we get a detailed account of the embrace of Augustus Gioovanni in WW 2805, pg 21-22. (Clanbook Cappadocian). And it is quite clear that the True Vessel contains the blood they tapped out of Augustus, his mortal blood. It is notable that the people who have been in posession of the True Vessel have seemed to be curiously immune to the hostility of Clan Giovanni (Samedi) or had them embark on projects they would approve of (Setites).<br /> <br /> Japeth did indeed create it though, and also seems to have put the clan curse on the Giovanni. He would have known exactly what it contained, unlike Augustus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once upon a time, long time ago, I read somewhere that the Vessel could be used to kill Augustus if he were to ever drink it - because it were his own mortal blood. Now, I dont remember where or how or why, but I do remember I read it.<br /> <br /> As for part of Cap's soul being left out from the diablerri, I think that's due to the necromancy powers that turned Cap into a Wraith (instead of history).<br /> <br /> Also, it's like I always say, nobody is ever really gone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T07:46:29-07:00","id":1487885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and just the same could be said about you. If that didnt bothered you, you clearly wouldnt be complaining like a child.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh yes, the company is within their rights to do whatever they please. Just dont complain about it when you see your sales drop semester after semester.<br /> <br /> Also, just because they are within their right, doesnt mean I must shut my mouth. Which is exactly what you would like people to do, you would want to forcefully shut the mouth of people who's opinions you dont like, but it doesnt work like that (so who's having a childish tantrum again?)<br /> <br /> As for the company, they are free to displease their costumers, all businesses are free to do that, but it's a really dumb way to conduct a business. And, the definite proof that White Wolf realized it's mistake and it realize that it cant force its costumers to do what it wants, is that they had to endure the shameful process of &quot;unending&quot; the world in order to try to keep their sales afloat.<br /> <br /> Now now dear, you need to learn how to deal with different opinions. The world doesnt orbit your enlightned person. And just because you like something, doesnt mean everybody else has to bow to your &quot;superior wisdom&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's the definition of childish tantrum, so if I were you, I'd be looking for a mirror.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Please leave the thread and take the day off.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:00:57-07:00","id":1487901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487863#post1487863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once upon a time, long time ago, I read somewhere that the Vessel could be used to kill Augustus if he were to ever drink it - because it were his own mortal blood. Now, I dont remember where or how or why, but I do remember I read it.<br /> <br /> As for part of Cap's soul being left out from the diablerri, I think that's due to the necromancy powers that turned Cap into a Wraith (instead of history).<br /> <br /> Also, it's like I always say, nobody is ever really gone...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never read that... but it is a perfect fit! The story of Augustus embrace includes a reference to Japheth seeing Augustus rotten soul with soulsight. Leaving a boobytrap that would only trigger if Augustus betrayed the Clan would get around Cappadocious commands, while being in accordance with his opinion of Augustus. And it explains why Japheth is so phlegmatic about Augustus gaining the True Vessel.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T11:36:49-07:00","id":1487923,"title":"","content":"That is an interesting take on the character, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\">AnubisXy</a></b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">. It seems like a lot of the jyhad involves plotting to cause a catastrophe. And a lot of these plots come from clans where the founder was destroyed, such as Tremere (the True Name of the entire human race) and the Hecate and arguably the Brujah (something involving the Bali). And of course the worst such plot comes from the Ventrue\u2026.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T23:10:58-07:00","id":1488764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1487923#post1487923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an interesting take on the character, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\">AnubisXy</a></b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">. It seems like a lot of the jyhad involves plotting to cause a catastrophe. And a lot of these plots come from clans where the founder was destroyed, such as Tremere (the True Name of the entire human race) and the Hecate and arguably the Brujah (something involving the Bali). And of course the worst such plot comes from the Ventrue\u2026.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious on that Ventrue plot you mentionned, I don't remember the Ventrue having a destructive overplot in the jyhad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T02:03:29-07:00","id":1488775,"title":"","content":"Nice write up. The only probably i have with the idea of Lazarus being close to winning the Jyhad is: ''What are the antes doing?'' They are just drinking their kool aid and allowing him to become a godlike figure?, create an army of wraith vampires? etc. You would think that atleast one of them would see the threath and decide to do something about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T13:05:00-07:00","id":1488872,"title":"","content":"Or maybe they have become so removed from there humanity Blackshade that they can't see a true threat anymore or they are waiting for the right moment to hijack Lazarus plan for there own end. They did that with Tremere in one the Gehenna options with Tmzsice asserting his presence at the right moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T19:30:59-07:00","id":1488923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1488775#post1488775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice write up. The only probably i have with the idea of Lazarus being close to winning the Jyhad is: ''What are the antes doing?'' They are just drinking their kool aid and allowing him to become a godlike figure?, create an army of wraith vampires? etc. You would think that atleast one of them would see the threath and decide to do something about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex 10 seem to be the most useless of the powers, given all the shenanigans of the lore that just go over their heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T10:38:10-07:00","id":1488989,"title":"","content":"somehow I always thought that only Cappadocius was knowledgeable crazy and powerful enough to &quot;become&quot; or eat god (same thing).<br /> So, in a way, I thought Lazarus actually wanted to ressurect the old man, not to do the apotheosis himself. And hot damn, bring a semi-diablerised Antediluvian back to unlife would be one hell of a plot. And one I think most of the non-Talmahera Kindred would go absolutely no no. Or you could go absolutely more bonkers and say that Lazarus wants to bring Cappadocius back, only so that HE can diablerise the bastard wholly himself. <br /> <br /> Either way, I love Cappadocians and the entire Clan of Death(s). I also personally feel like both Jappeth and Lazarus and to a lesser degree Byzar (which feel a bit too remote to be part of it) kinda of amalgamated their souls into a single amazingly powerful being. Something that might be akin to a diablerie, but isn't that. That would make the Cappuchin have all the reasons to be a total power god. Maybe each of the Methuselah want something different, and at critical points, they fight internally for control, since they meshed voluntarily, and so there aint a stronger entity (if there was it would have to be Lazarus). Maybe Jappeth just wants to bring back his father, so that he can bring Heaven on Earth. Maybe Lazarus wants to devour Cappadocius once he becomes whole. Maybe Bayzar wants to use the mantle of the Cappuchin just so he can steal enlightened souls for himself, and bring him closer to Golconda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T17:01:31-07:00","id":1489032,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Japheth, I am told (I have not personally read these sources) that the leader of the Harbingers of Skulls was his childe, and she claims Japheth himself set them free.<br /> <br /> You touch on the fact that Lazarus-as-Capuchin asked for Claudius Giovanni's remains. I like the idea that Lazarus manipulated Augustus into killing his brother's diablerist and into giving him his corpse. I'd say he could have brought Japheth back through Claudius, and thus another face of the Capuchin was born","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27519-royalmudcrab","name":"RoyalMudcrab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T18:54:46-07:00","id":1489177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They did that with Tremere in one the Gehenna options with Tmzsice asserting his presence at the right moment. </div> </div> </div>Which was, by the way, one of the worst scenarios of Gehenna (even though it's hard to decide, given that all of them are terrible). They made Tzimisce so ridiculously op in the Gehenna that it makes me want to have him destroyed in one of my games, just so that I feel &quot;justice&quot; has been done, lol.<br /> <br /> I'm really enjoying the discussion about Lazarus here, I think he's one of the most interesting characters in the WoD and one that has a lot of potential for stories, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T09:39:45-07:00","id":1489345,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Herr Meister;n1489177]<br /> <br /> Which was, by the way, one of the worst scenarios of Gehenna (even though it's hard to decide, given that all of them are terrible). They made Tzimisce so ridiculously op in the Gehenna that it makes me want to have him destroyed in one of my games, just so that I feel &quot;justice&quot; has been done, lol.<br /> <br /> I know he kept popping up in numerous Gehenna scenarios and was becoming like Kenny from South Park.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T02:52:32-07:00","id":1489616,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Lysander;n1489345]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1489177#post1489177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which was, by the way, one of the worst scenarios of Gehenna (even though it's hard to decide, given that all of them are terrible). They made Tzimisce so ridiculously op in the Gehenna that it makes me want to have him destroyed in one of my games, just so that I feel &quot;justice&quot; has been done, lol.<br /> <br /> I know he kept popping up in numerous Gehenna scenarios and was becoming like Kenny from South Park.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I really couldn't understand the obsession the writers had with him! I swear I'm going to have him destroyed or subjugated in one of my games lol<br /> To this day, I still feel angry about the fact he was so &quot;omnipresent&quot;. I used to like him, but Gehenna really made me hate him back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T18:48:12-07:00","id":1489699,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Herr Meister;n1489616]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1489345#post1489345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, I really couldn't understand the obsession the writers had with him! I swear I'm going to have him destroyed or subjugated in one of my games lol<br /> To this day, I still feel angry about the fact he was so &amp;quot;omnipresent&amp;quot;. I used to like him, but Gehenna really made me hate him back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce and Saulot. Absolutely everywhere. Horrible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T19:03:23-07:00","id":1489700,"title":"","content":"Yeah<br /> There is the Eldest in so many places I had a Topic about where he is. Or where are his many pieces.<br /> So there is one in the America, and that is a big continent so anything goes.<br /> There is one in Damek Ruthven's possession in the form of a tree, maybe.<br /> I think there might be something in the Cathedral of Flesh.<br /> There was the Eldest in Tremere somehow.<br /> Also, the Eldest scramble in America might be Lugoj, but it might not too (so there would be another one).<br /> There is also the whole thing of the Eldest supposedly living throughout all of his brood too...<br /> So yeah, who needs Auspex when you can be everywhere.<br /> <br /> Saulot gets in way too many dishes for my taste, but not that much.<br /> You know a character that I like, that also might carry the Eldest, and is practically in every single material of the Dark Ages? That's Vykos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T10:22:25-07:00","id":1489755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1489699#post1489699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tzimisce and Saulot. Absolutely everywhere. Horrible</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce, Saulot and Tremere.<br /> <br /> Yes, it was fun at first, but the magic dream team trio became annoying as hell. The writters became too enthusiastic with that story, and could no longer drop the bone when they had to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T14:04:24-07:00","id":1489786,"title":"","content":"I like the Cappadocians as a clan. I like many of the NPCs of the clan. And I like much of the lore behind them.<br /> <br /> However, one thing I have never liked is how active the Cappadocian antedeluvian is, and how ancient and active so many of his childer are. According to official Lore, Japheth was over 8000 years old and still active at the time of the Conspiracy of Isaac. That is very different from how the other clans and their methusalehs are portrayed. It's a jarring element of the setting since we have to make an exception for him that isn't as present in the other clans.<br /> <br /> Some of the other clans have similar problems - primarily the Lasombra and Tzimisce. I guess this is what happens when the game tries to deal with the events of the Anarch Revolt and the diablerie of some of the antedeluvians at this time.<br /> <br /> I would be a lot less bothered if they pushed some of these characters down a generation or two, and included more flavor text on how certain ancients had only recently woke from torpor and were not known to be active. That's how I would handle it in my own chronicles. I just prefer certain powerful generations who were embraced long, long ago (like in the Bronze Age or earlier) to simply not be active. If a character is over 2000-3000 years old, it should be sleeping somewhere safely in torpor UNLESS it's recently woke up.<br /> <br /> So I think Lazarus is fine as a character, but I'd probably make him a 5th or even 6th generation vampire who was a doted, precocious &quot;grandchilde&quot; or so of Cappadocious rather than a favorite childe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:55:14-07:00","id":1489927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He gave his arguments. And the argument is that it's a ponzi scheme, which is a misconception</div> </div> </div> </div>It was less an argument and more an opinion given in a simplified form.<br /> <br /> And I personally think that while not technically true, it is a pretty good way of describing A) many schemes to attract people to crypto, regardless of their developers' intents and B) the effective result in how it gained tract as a financial asset (it mostly failed as actual money outside extremely niche situations, many of dubious purpose).<br /> <br /> So, while technically false, such an assertion isn't wrong as a passing, colloquial comment, as it may be just a simplification of a more complex opinion that wasn't being presented in full precisely because it was just a side comment. You can't assume too much from such a comment unless you full on start this conversation, and you're almost doing that the more you ask not to. If you want to drop it, just drop it. As you can see, I don't particularly want to, but I'm really trying to be nice and give you a chance to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:39:58-07:00","id":1489946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your baseless misconceptions about cryptos are politically driven, and if I were to explain why you are wrong it would also be politically driven, not to mention that this is not the topic. Hence why I asked you not to go on that subject.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing political in my disdain of Cryptos.<br /> <br /> And all of the things I've said, from the gap of wealth among it's possessors, to it's ecological impact, to it's effective uselessness, are not opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T19:56:51-07:00","id":1489989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1489946#post1489946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nothing political in my disdain of Cryptos.<br /> <br /> And all of the things I've said, from the gap of wealth among it's possessors, to it's ecological impact, to it's effective uselessness, are not opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why I dont wish to engage in politics is that I know myself enough to know that it wouldnt end well. As to why it would be a political discussion, is because it is. For example, that idea about ecology, which I know what is about, is false. And there's a very big reason as to why governments, mainstream media and the establishment is so vitriolic against cryptos, and the reason is political.<br /> <br /> Im more than willing to talk about that, but not in this thread, because first it is derailing it too much, but I would gladly talk about ideas relating the VAs to the creating of cryptos (or even the Syndicate, if you're willing to engage in conspiracy theories and to claim that cryptos are a new big evil), but exclusively in the context of the game (Mage in this case), and only regarding any technical doubts about it and only if those would relate to the game, and leaving all the political considerations aside - and there are MANY political considerations regarding cryptos.<br /> <br /> I've already took a few (well deserved by the way) strikes in these forums, and Im not willing to stirr the hornets nests anymore, so I dont think it's such a good idea for me to go in those discussions. But, like I said, Im willing to discuss it, but exclusively if it's game related.<br /> <br /> And please, if it is really your wish, make a new thread for it, and let us let the rest of the viewers return to the OP's thread and end this derailing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T11:37:00-07:00","id":1490042,"title":"","content":"Cryptocurrency <i>is</i> political. It is political in the same way Citizens United is, in that it allows for dark money transfers.<br /> <br /> Has anyone here read the short story in the <i>first</i> Giovanni Clanbook, the one with the snuff filmmaker who has to go to the Giovanni to handle his income because banks wouldn't touch him? The banks wouldn't touch him because his money would be traced to his business. Cryptocurrency, <i>if it worked as advertised</i>, would have solved that little problem. The &quot;Crypto&quot; part of Cryptocurrency is meant to imply secrecy, that people can't tell where it's come from or where it's going. It is the <i>definition</i> of dark money and the Giovanni snuff film guy would have loved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T12:42:52-07:00","id":1490047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1490042#post1490042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Crypto&quot; part of Cryptocurrency is meant to imply secrecy,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's indeed a misconception, actually.<br /> <br /> &quot;Crypto&quot; in cryptocurrency refers just to the fact that it uses a cryptographic system that relies on the community of users itself instead of a certifying authority. This is a purely technical reference.<br /> <br /> And while this use as &quot;<i>dark money&quot;</i> does exist and has a number of defenders, the actual technology does the opposite: it makes the validation chain of transaction public, which means that anyone can audit the entire life of every unit at any time with little effort (the transfer must be certified by cryptography, the log itself isn't encrypted).<br /> <br /> What makes anonymity possible is that while the <i>wallets</i> that hold them are identified, <i>the owners aren't</i>. But this isn't any technical challenge, requirement or anything, it is just a fact of the basic system as much as the basic system of your computer identifies your equipment by a unique code, but has no built-in slot to say it belongs to you. You can literally solve this with a spreadsheet.<br /> <br /> If you note down somewhere who's the owner of a wallet, something many Exchanges already do to keep track of their customers and offer some services and safety, then there is no anonymity. A government requiring an Exchange to record this information is completely feasible. Outlawing ownership or trade with unidentified wallets is perfectly doable, and actually easy to implement due to the public aspect of the chain. That's why China is investing in developing its own state owned Crypto, because it will be stupidly easy for the government to track everything.<br /> <br /> However you feel about the matter of privacy on that, and despite the system being intended to make the transaction itself impossible to stop (because it has no central register), granting privacy is not the goal of the system itself and it actually needs the opposite to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T20:12:24-07:00","id":1490089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1490047#post1490047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's indeed a misconception, actually.<br /> <br /> &quot;Crypto&quot; in cryptocurrency refers just to the fact that it uses a cryptographic system that relies on the community of users itself instead of a certifying authority. This is a purely technical reference.<br /> <br /> And while this use as &quot;<i>dark money&quot;</i> does exist and has a number of defenders, the actual technology does the opposite: it makes the validation chain of transaction public, which means that anyone can audit the entire life of every unit at any time with little effort (the transfer must be certified by cryptography, the log itself isn't encrypted).<br /> <br /> What makes anonymity possible is that while the <i>wallets</i> that hold them are identified, <i>the owners aren't</i>. But this isn't any technical challenge, requirement or anything, it is just a fact of the basic system as much as the basic system of your computer identifies your equipment by a unique code, but has no built-in slot to say it belongs to you. You can literally solve this with a spreadsheet.<br /> <br /> If you note down somewhere who's the owner of a wallet, something many Exchanges already do to keep track of their customers and offer some services and safety, then there is no anonymity. A government requiring an Exchange to record this information is completely feasible. Outlawing ownership or trade with unidentified wallets is perfectly doable, and actually easy to implement due to the public aspect of the chain. That's why China is investing in developing its own state owned Crypto, because it will be stupidly easy for the government to track everything.<br /> <br /> However you feel about the matter of privacy on that, and despite the system being intended to make the transaction itself impossible to stop (because it has no central register), granting privacy is not the goal of the system itself and it actually needs the opposite to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>OH.<br /> <br /> Well, then, somebody's got to explain <i>all</i> of this to the Far-Right up here in Canada, because they are all over cryptocurrency. The anti-masking convoys earlier this year were using it for funding, the disgraced Premier of my province tried to pump up cryptocurrency as an industry to invest tax dollars in, and the &quot;rising star&quot; of the national conservative party endorsed bitcoin <i>just</i> before it crashed the hardest it's ever done. <br /> <br /> I guess snuff film guy should stick to &quot;banking&quot; his money with the Giovanni...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T19:48:59-07:00","id":1490212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1490089#post1490089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH.<br /> <br /> Well, then, somebody's got to explain <i>all</i> of this to the Far-Right up here in Canada,</div> </div> </div> </div>Somebody has to explain all that to the far-right everywhere, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of cryptos myself, and there's much more about them, good and bad. And yes, a lot of people believe they're about hiding your transactions. Indeed, many of the developers that know it isn't about that still want to achieve this goal anyway, they're anarchists and don't believe that any government or institution should be able to watch your transactions.<br /> <br /> My comment was exclusively about the technical aspect. The &quot;crypto&quot; there refer to a key technical element. And ironically, this element actually works wonderfully to break anonymity when society starts to make actual rules and laws for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T10:47:14-07:00","id":1490271,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Lazarus sure has a lot of relation with all of this.<br /> I'm sure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T10:48:35-07:00","id":1490272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1490271#post1490271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Lazarus sure has a lot of relation with all of this.<br /> I'm sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to end this derailing... More or less.<br /> <br /> Now, if we could finally go back to talk about Lazaru's shenanigans...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T17:41:08-07:00","id":1507631,"title":"","content":"I still want to know. What is ventrues big evil plan?<br /> <br /> Hecata become God<br /> Tzimisce steals the names of humanity or whatever<br /> Tremere also steal humanities name?<br /> Brujah drag in baaali<br /> Nosferatu destroys his own line","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T18:55:48-07:00","id":1507731,"title":"","content":"That's like asking what Jeff Bezos' big, evil plan is, or Richard Branson, or Aristotle Onassis, or J. Paul Getty.<br /> <br /> Power for something <i>other</i> than the sake of power would be more of a twist than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T07:23:08-07:00","id":1508030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1507731#post1507731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's like asking what Jeff Bezos' big, evil plan is, or Richard Branson, or Aristotle Onassis, or J. Paul Getty.<br /> <br /> Power for something <i>other</i> than the sake of power would be more of a twist than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really liked this simple idea. Revised went out of its way to give certain Antediluvians a &quot;m\u00e1ster plan&quot; or &quot;endgame&quot; and blatantly ignored the ones who didn't have one (like Ventrue or Arikel). The way I imagine the Antediluvians, they are just human beings (very old and powerful, but just human beings) who just want what humans want: to have power, to control things, to survive... and have no master plan or endgame, they don't know if Gehenna will ever come or it's a myth. They just move night to night, trapped in an eternal struggle with no end in sight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T23:36:26-07:00","id":1508117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1508030#post1508030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really liked this simple idea. Revised went out of its way to give certain Antediluvians a &quot;m\u00e1ster plan&quot; or &quot;endgame&quot; and blatantly ignored the ones who didn't have one (like Ventrue or Arikel). The way I imagine the Antediluvians, they are just human beings (very old and powerful, but just human beings) who just want what humans want: to have power, to control things, to survive... and have no master plan or endgame, they don't know if Gehenna will ever come or it's a myth. They just move night to night, trapped in an eternal struggle with no end in sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is perfectly acceptable for an important and legendary Vampire like a Founder ( Arikel, for example ) , or one of the senior 4th Generation Kindred , to have no need for a grand, exclusive, mystical ( and possibly transhumanist or radical ) plan or approach.<br /> <br /> This still leaves room for various occult goals and personal ambitions, including these that would matter for whole groups and societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T00:10:44-07:00","id":1508123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487590-some-thoughts-on-lazarus?p=1508117#post1508117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is perfectly acceptable for an important and legendary Vampire like a Founder ( Arikel, for example ) , or one of the senior 4th Generation Kindred , to have no need for a grand, exclusive, mystical ( and possibly transhumanist or radical ) plan or approach.<br /> <br /> This still leaves room for various occult goals and personal ambitions, including these that would matter for whole groups and societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. In my game, Mithras is am example of this. During the glory of Rome, when he was an Elder, he approached the Senate but was somewhat rejected as a foreigner, so he promised he would one night rule the mightiest empire on the world. So he schemed and planned and plotted for almost two millennia to get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T01:56:13-07:00","id":1508260,"title":"","content":"The problem with mentioning certain topics is that they *do* bring in spammers. I'd suggest avoiding those terms if you don't want the forums to be full of not-so-subtle guerilla marketing.<br /> <br /> Watch out for posts that almost make sense with their use of a few carefully selected &quot;in-group&quot; words, or do make sense but are tangential at best, but which nevertheless casually manage to slip in a link to a spammy website.<br /> <br /> Realistically, most of us would not be linking to external sites selling things when talking about this stuff in the context of the WoD. There would be no need to. Always be suspicious of someone who does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T09:17:28-07:00","id":1508535,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Yeah, discussing crypto on these forums is a banned topic. Whatever your opinion on it, let alone advertising it. Deleted the relevant posts.<br /> <br /> No one is banned or getting an infraction for it but it is a topic that has a <i>history</i> on the forums.<br /> <br /> Please go back to Lazarus.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-